  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Batik Wastewater Solutions, Pekalongan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the project is to develop solutions for waste water management for the batik industry in Pekalongan city, Indonesia, to reduce environmental pollution and to improve the water footprint of the batik workshops. The activities will contribute to the cooperation in water between Indonesia and the Netherlands and create opportunities for Dutch businesses in Indonesia.In a wider ongoing cooperation between the Netherlands and Pekalongan, the city will be supported with improvements for the urban water (quality) management system in an integrated manner. Assistance will be provided with setting up suitable waste-water treatment and water re-use facilities (technical installation, management and operation skills). This cooperation, including local government and the Indonesian private sector (batik and textile companies), has the potential to create business opportunities for Dutch companies.</narrative>
  </description>
